  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABHYeLxw",
      "title": "proxyd: add opt-in rate limiting by authenticated alias",
      "author": "bitwiseguy",
      "number": 761,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAddresses task 3 of this [RPC Hardening notion doc](https://app.notion.com/p/oplabs/RPC-Hardening-Work-Planning-3e6f153ee16280ea8fb8c3bc66ea4789).\r\n\r\nAdd opt-in `[rate_limit] use_auth_alias` so authenticated consumers sharing an egress IP get independent rate-limit buckets.\r\n\r\nBase and method limits use the configured alias across HTTP requests, batch elements, and mapped WebSocket calls, with isolated buckets in memory and Redis. Unauthenticated requests retain IP-based limits. Default behavior and existing exemptions remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\nNew tests added that cover...\r\n\r\n- Independent quotas for different aliases sharing an IP.\r\n- Shared quotas across IPs and credentials using the same alias.\r\n- Disabled-mode compatibility and alias/IP bucket isolation.\r\n- Redis quota sharing across replicas.\r\n- Batch rejection handling and HTTP/WS quota sharing.\r\n- Rejection metrics attributed by alias.\r\n\r\nThe full proxyd test suite and focused race checks passed.\r\n\r\n## Related Issues\r\n\r\n* Closes https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/core-team/issues/3251\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T17:18:54Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T20:37:39Z",
      "additions": 462,
      "deletions": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ86dMUyf",
      "title": "feat(proxyd): add flashblocks-aware routing",
      "author": "paranoiacblack",
      "number": 418,
      "body": "**Description**\r\n\r\n- Adds flashblocks-aware routing. When `eth_getBlockByNumber`, `eth_getTransactionCount`, `eth_getTransactionReceipt` and `eth_getBalance` are called with \"pending\" block numbers on chains producing Flashblocks, the request will be answered by a flashblocks-aware backend.\r\n- Adds configuration that enables flashblocks-aware routing.\r\n- Adds configuration that allows specifying exactly one flashblocks-aware backend group.\r\n- Adds logic to parse JSON-RPC request's method and parameters to determine if it should be sent to the flashblocks-aware backend group or to normally configured backend group for the rpc method mapping. \r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\n- Added tests for checking for pending JSON-RPC requests.\r\n- Added integration tests for every request + param combination that can ask for information about the latest flashblock.\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2025-07-03T04:11:39Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 348,
      "deletions": 65
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABNCLxpQ",
      "title": "ci: release Go binaries from GitHub Actions",
      "author": "falcorocks",
      "number": 793,
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add a `release-go-binaries` GitHub Actions workflow. It runs on `<module>/v*` tags for `op-signer`, `op-txproxy`, `op-ufm`, `proxyd`, `op-conductor-mon`, `peer-mgmt-service` and `cci-stats`, and on `workflow_dispatch` for an existing tag.\n- The build job runs with read-only permissions and builds the archives and `<module>_<version>_checksums.txt` for linux/amd64, darwin/amd64, darwin/arm64 and windows/amd64. The publish job has `contents: write` and runs no repository code. It only attaches the uploaded artifacts to a draft release and then publishes it.\n- Archive and checksum names are the same as before.\n- Behaviour changes: binaries are static (`CGO_ENABLED=0`). Versions with a `-` suffix are marked as prereleases. Release notes are the module's commit log since its previous tag. `op-txproxy` releases are not marked as latest.\n- Remove the CircleCI `go-release` job and its release workflow, along with the seven per-module `.goreleaser.yaml` files. `RELEASE.md` is updated to describe the tag-driven process.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-05T10:02:52Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-05T10:19:12Z",
      "additions": 264,
      "deletions": 508
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABN67PNQ",
      "title": "enable tx validation trace logging",
      "author": "yashvardhan-kukreja",
      "number": 797,
      "body": "Signed-off-by: Yashvardhan Kukreja <yashvardhan@oplabs.co>\r\n\r\n<!-- Contributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md -->\r\n\r\n**Description**\r\n\r\nAdds two Info logs to each tx validation request, emitted from `httptrace` hooks: `tx validation conn queued` when the request starts waiting for a pooled connection, and `tx validation got conn` with `conn_queued_ms` when it gets one. \r\n\r\nBoth carry `req_id`. This helps troubleshoot tx validation timeouts during traffic bursts by showing whether the time went to the connection pool (a `conn queued` with no `got conn`) or to the tx validation middleware (`got conn`, then a timeout).\r\n\r\nI chose logs over metrics because per-request timing is detailed enough for troubleshooting but too detailed to alert on or chart trends from, and Info level because two short lines per request adds little log volume.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\nPlease describe any tests you've added. If you've added no tests, or left important behavior untested, please explain why not.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nAdd any other context about the problem you're solving.\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\n- Fixes #[Link to Issue]\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-09T18:39:42Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T19:01:51Z",
      "additions": 95,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABLz0nRA",
      "title": "feat(proxyd): add auth label to latency, cache and HTTP status metrics",
      "author": "jelias2",
      "number": 791,
      "body": "## Summary\nPer-API-key observability already exists on nine metrics via the `auth` label (the alias configured in `[authentication]`, or `none`). This extends it to the remaining request-scoped metrics so latency, cache hit rate and HTTP status can be filtered per key:\n\n- `proxyd_http_request_by_method_duration_seconds` (`method_name`, `auth`)\n- `proxyd_cache_hits_total` / `proxyd_cache_misses_total` (`method`, `auth`)\n- `proxyd_http_response_codes_total` (`status_code`, `auth`)\n\nUnauthenticated and rejected (401) requests carry `auth=\"none\"`, same as the existing metrics.\n\n### Cardinality\nEach metric gains one series per configured key alias. For the latency histogram that is methods × keys × 12 buckets, so fine for tens of keys; worth reconsidering for hundreds.\n\n### Dashboards\nExisting queries keep working since `auth` is additive, but any panel that does not aggregate (`sum by (...)`) will now show one line per key.\n\n## Test plan\n- New `TestHTTPRequestByMethodDurationAuthLabel` asserts an authenticated request lands in the `auth=\"alice\"` series for both the histogram and the status counter.\n- Existing tests pinned to `auth=\"none\"` so superset label matching stays unambiguous.\n- `go test ./...` passes in `proxyd/`.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-30T16:20:11Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 53,
      "deletions": 18
    }
